       "content": {
        "id": "v2-proposal-j3-222534-root",
        "type": "question",
        "label": null,
        "prompt": "Use the diagonals to decide whether each quadrilateral is a rectangle, a rhombus or a square.",
        "children": [
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-222534-j3-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "$A(4,5)$, $B(-4,1)$, $C(-2,-3)$ and $D(6,1)$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 60,
          "answer": {
           "short": "Rectangle: $AC=BD=10$, both midpoints are $(1,1)$, and $m_{AC}=\\frac43$, $m_{BD}=0$ are not perpendicular.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AC&=\\sqrt{(-2-4)^2+(-3-5)^2}=10\\\\BD&=\\sqrt{(6-(-4))^2+(1-1)^2}=10\\\\M_{AC}&=\\left(\\frac{4+(-2)}{2},\\frac{5+(-3)}{2}\\right)=(1,1)\\\\M_{BD}&=\\left(\\frac{-4+6}{2},\\frac{1+1}{2}\\right)=(1,1)\\\\m_{AC}&=\\frac{-3-5}{-2-4}=\\frac43\\\\m_{BD}&=\\frac{1-1}{6-(-4)}=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe diagonals are equal and bisect each other, but $m_{AC}\\times m_{BD}=0\\ne-1$, so they are not perpendicular. $ABCD$ is a rectangle."
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-222534-j3-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "$P(4,2)$, $Q(-1,3)$, $R(-2,-2)$ and $S(3,-3)$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 60,
          "answer": {
           "short": "Square: $PR=QS=\\sqrt{52}$, both midpoints are $(1,0)$, and $m_{PR}=\\frac23$, $m_{QS}=-\\frac32$ have product $-1$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}PR&=\\sqrt{(-2-4)^2+(-2-2)^2}=\\sqrt{52}\\\\QS&=\\sqrt{(3-(-1))^2+(-3-3)^2}=\\sqrt{52}\\\\M_{PR}&=\\left(\\frac{4+(-2)}{2},\\frac{2+(-2)}{2}\\right)=(1,0)\\\\M_{QS}&=\\left(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{3+(-3)}{2}\\right)=(1,0)\\\\m_{PR}&=\\frac{-2-2}{-2-4}=\\frac23\\\\m_{QS}&=\\frac{-3-3}{3-(-1)}=-\\frac32\\\\m_{PR}\\times m_{QS}&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nThe diagonals are equal, bisect each other and are perpendicular, so $PQRS$ is a square."
          }
         }
        ],
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2
